    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a helpful analogy. To round this out, can you touch on how we actually automate this in AWS? We're looking specifically at Auto Scaling groups. How does the system decide when to trigger those new instances in a horizontal setup? I want to make sure the stakeholders understand that it's not just a manual process we do whenever we feel like it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In AWS, Auto Scaling groups automate horizontal scaling based on predefined metrics rather than manual intervention. The system constantly monitors key performance indicators, such as CPU utilization or request queue length. If these metrics cross a specified threshold, the Auto Scaling group automatically launches new instances to distribute the load, ensuring performance remains consistent. This ensures our infrastructure scales proactively and reliably to meet fluctuating demand.",
      "source": "target",
